 ## Background
-The Fragment List-Based Rendering Pipeline was developed as part of the "Smoker" application for real-time smoke volume rendering. It was chosen over raytracing techniques to maintain accuracy and avoid issues related to self-intersections and global intersections [S1, unofficial]. The pipeline generalizes the rendering process into four distinct stages executed by three shader programs (Clear, Render, Display) [S1, unofficial].
+The method was developed for the "Smoker" application, a real-time smoke volume rendering system. It was presented in a master's thesis by Sowinski in 2012 [S1, unofficial]. The pipeline was chosen to provide a flexible framework allowing runtime switching between different rendering strategies without re-initializing the smoke volume, facilitating comparison of approaches under identical configurations [S1, unofficial].
 
